Their interface works very well for actual Google Groups just like the
Yahoo interface works very well for actual Yahoo Groups.  In both cases
that's their motivator.

There appears to be a gateway in place to make UseNet visible using the
Google Groups interface.  It does not appear they take the behavior of
that interface into account *at all* as they develop how it works with
their own groups.

Folks on UseNet don't like this approach at all but I don't think the
Google development team even tries to test against it.  It's an internal
product that is designed to and tested against their own internal groups
and I am convinced that's how they view it.


